# Dependencies
node_modules
# npm writes a temporary `.node_modules-<hash>` symlink during install and
# leaves it behind if the install is interrupted. The name does not match the
# `node_modules` pattern above, so it is NOT ignored -- and `git add -A` will
# happily commit a broken symlink into the repo. Nearly shipped one on
# 2026-08-23.
.node_modules-*

# Build
dist
# The native (Capacitor) bundle. Rebuilt by `npm run build:native`, copied
# into ios/ and android/ by `cap sync`; never published as the web bundle.
dist-native
coverage

# Vercel
.vercel

# Supabase
supabase/.temp

# Environment — NEVER track any .env file with real secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.check

# Secrets that are not .env files (2026-08-21). A token was saved to
# github_token.md beside the .env, untracked but NOT ignored - one `git add -A`
# from any of the agents that run here constantly would have committed it.
# GitHub auto-revokes leaked tokens, so the damage is an outage, not just an
# exposure. Ignore the shapes, not one filename.
github_token.md
*token*.md
*secret*.md
*credentials*.md
.env.vercel
.env.prod.check

# IDE
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
# Generated PioSolver trees (regeneratable)
scripts/trees/
server/vitest.config.ts.timestamp-*.mjs

# Debug/test build outputs (e.g. dist-bug021, dist-hotfix, etc.)
# These are one-off build snapshots that agents create during debugging.
# They contain 500+ files each and cause VS Code to show 1K+ phantom changes.
dist-*/
dist.dead.*/
.vercel/output/
*.local

# Agent brain artifacts (may contain tokens, session data)
.gemini/

# Agent memory/context files (tracked selectively, not bulk)
# Uncomment below if you want to gitignore all .memory files:
# .memory/
.ssh/

*.stale.*
**/*.stale.*/

# Round 19 — local-only artifacts that shouldn't ship
.agent/openclaw-dispatcher-live-*.py
playwright-report/
# Playwright failure artifacts: screenshots, videos, trace zips. 4.2 MB after a
# single failing run, and only playwright-report/ was ignored - so any blanket
# Broad staging could commit these shared-worktree artifacts accidentally.
test-results/

# Scratch/quarantine dir. device_bash on the mounted volume cannot unlink,
# so stale locks and old build dirs get parked here instead of deleted.
_to_delete/

# Staging area for moving code between the sandbox and the host. Held a 12 MB
# ca-code.tgz that a blanket `git add -A` would otherwise have committed.
.upload-scratch/
# One-off Playwright probe scripts written to the repo root while debugging.
_v*.mjs

# Scratch space for ad-hoc production probes (screenshots, one-off .mjs).
# The COMMITTED walkthrough suite is e2e-live/ — 4.4 MB of throwaway probes and
# a 232-line-stale duplicate of multitable-walk.mjs were tracked here, which is
# exactly how the next person edits the wrong copy.
e2e-work/

# Playwright's authenticated storageState, written fresh by
# tests/e2e/global-setup.ts on every run. Never commit a session token.
tests/e2e/.auth/

# FUSE mount artifacts. The Cowork/device sandbox mounts this repo over FUSE,
# which cannot unlink a file that is still open — the kernel renames it to
# .fuse_hiddenXXXXXXXX instead and leaves it behind. Three of these were sitting
# untracked in src/ on 2026-08-21, one `git add -A` away from being committed.
# They are never source. Same story as _to_delete/ above.
.fuse_hidden*

# One-off debug screenshots dropped at the repo root (_cards_probe.png, etc).
# The committed visual suite is e2e-live/; these are throwaways.
_*_probe.png

# Ad-hoc one-shot Python rewriters dropped at the repo root while iterating on
# CSS/JSX (patch_cardimage.py, update_css.py, ...). They encode a single edit
# that has already been applied and are meaningless afterwards, but `git add -A`
# will happily commit them. The durable form of such a change is the diff it
# produced, not the script that produced it.
/patch_*.py
/update_css.py
/fix_*.py

# Root-level probe leftovers: bare screenshots and dotfile scratch written by
# ad-hoc production checks. Same rationale as _*_probe.png above.
/.e2e.png
/.ca_probe_*

# PERF PASS 2026-08-22: build-time WebP variants of the card-face PNGs,
# generated by scripts/generate-webp-media.mjs during `npm run build`.
# Regenerable artifacts — never commit (agents push via GitHub MCP which
# cannot carry binaries anyway). The committed .webp under cards/backs/
# are source assets and are NOT matched by these patterns.
public/cards/2color/*.webp
public/cards/4color/*.webp

# Merge/patch artifacts. Committed to main on 2026-08-22 by #262 — six of them,
# including two .rej files, which mean `patch` REJECTED those hunks. The hunks
# were later applied by hand so the feature is fine, but a .rej in src/ is a
# rejected change sitting in the tree looking like source, and the next agent
# to grep for `clock` finds it twice. Never committable again.
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak

# Agent scratch. Never shipped; kept out of the tree so a `git add -A`
# cannot sweep a probe file or a staging directory into main (it did, twice:
# 19 files were tracked on main by 2026-08-23).
_agent_tmp/

# More of the same, found untracked in the working tree on 2026-08-23 while
# preparing a push. Stage only explicit task-owned paths so anything sitting
# here cannot become source accidentally. These are all
# one-off probes and staging dirs, not code:
#   _to_delete/      quarantine for files the sandbox mount cannot unlink
#   .cowork-trees/   per-agent worktrees
#   test_db*.mjs     ad-hoc Supabase connectivity checks
#   patch_*.cjs/.js  single-use codemods that have already been applied
_to_delete/
.cowork-trees/
/check-locks.cjs
/workspace-cmd.sh
/test-query.cjs
/test_db*.mjs
/patch_*.cjs
/patch_*.js
.git-msg-*.txt

# Agent worktrees created by scripts/agent-workspace.sh. These are live git
# worktrees, not build output: they must never be committed, and leaving them
# untracked makes the shared clone read dirty forever, which is how a clone
# ends up stranded on a rescue branch with real work mixed into the noise.
.agent-trees/

# Python bytecode from dev scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.dr-backups/

# ── Agent scratch that keeps landing in the shared clone ──────────────────
# Found 2026-09-02 in ~/Documents/club-arena: a 5.8MB arm64 `actionlint`
# binary sitting untracked and UNIGNORED in the repo root, next to a
# `pr_list.txt` and a `scan-labels.tmp.mjs`, left behind by the Actions cost
# audit. One `git add -A` from anybody and the binary is in the history for
# good, and history is the one place you cannot delete a 5.8MB mistake from
# cheaply.
#
# The tools themselves are fine to download - pin them here rather than ask
# every agent to remember to clean up after itself, which is the instruction
# that has never once worked.
/actionlint
/pr_list.txt
/scan-labels.tmp.mjs
*.tmp.mjs

# Written by the entry-module-manifest plugin in vite.config.ts each build;
# read by scripts/ci/entry-chunk-delta.mjs. Build output, never committed.
.entry-modules.json

# MIGRATION-RESERVATION TEST DEBRIS (2026-09-05).
# tests/a-migration-version-is-reserved-not-guessed.law.test.ts has to write
# real files into supabase/migrations/ - that is the only way the reservation
# script can see those seconds as taken - and it removes them in a `finally`.
# A run that is interrupted never reaches the finally, and the next `git add -A`
# commits the leftovers. That is not hypothetical: 197 of them reached main
# through three separate pull requests, and one took the exact version another
# agent's real migration had reserved, turning CI red for work that was correct
# when it was written. Supabase keys schema_migrations on the version, so of two
# files sharing one the second is SILENTLY NEVER APPLIED - the collision is
# worse than the red build it causes.
supabase/migrations/*_squatter_holding_this_second.sql
supabase/migrations/*_the_first_agent_reserves_a_name.sql
supabase/migrations/*_the_second_agent_reserves_a_name.sql
supabase/migrations/*_a_second_agent_wants_the_same_second.sql

# The migration-reservation law test writes its fixtures here instead of
# supabase/migrations/, so they cannot race the dozen test files that scan that
# directory. See tests/a-migration-version-is-reserved-not-guessed.law.test.ts.
.tmp-migration-reservation-probe/
infra/monitoring/.deployed-from
.throwable-sources/
.throwable-darkroom/

# Visual-harness screenshots are build output, not source.
tests/visual/__shots__/

# Release-journal test Postgres clusters. Each run of the release-journal
# suite initdb's a throwaway cluster into work/release-journal-pg-<random>/
# and leaves it behind. Untracked and unignored, they are indistinguishable
# from real untracked work in `git status`: the 2026-09-18 work-at-risk survey
# found 389,960 such files across the agent worktrees - 8.3 GB in three trees
# alone - burying the handful of genuinely unsaved edits sitting beside them.
# That is how uncommitted work gets lost: not deleted, just never noticed.
work/release-journal-pg-*/
